   "source": [
    "### 7c. Batch-correctie (voor visualisatie en ML)\n",
    "Het artikel gebruikte *bridged* en *intensity-normalised* NPX, waarbij batch-effecten al verwijderd waren. Bij onze data is dat duidelijk niet het geval.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Waarom niet gewoon per batch centreren?** Batch is verstrengeld met leeftijd (7b). Als je elke batch op hetzelfde gemiddelde zet, verwijder je ook een deel van het echte leeftijdseffect.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Onze aanpak, in de geest van `limma::removeBatchEffect`:** per eiwit fitten we een lineair model\n",
    "`NPX ~ batch + age group + sex + CMV`\n",
    "en trekken we enkel het batch-deel af. De biologische variabelen staan in het model, zodat hun effect *beschermd* wordt.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Toepassing | Wat gebruiken we? |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| Regressie in deel 2 en 3 | **Ongecorrigeerde** NPX, met **batch als covariaat** in het model. Dat is statistisch het eerlijkst. |\n",
    "| PCA, figuren en machine learning (deel 4) | **Batch-gecorrigeerde** NPX |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 27,
   "id": "1455aad7",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-11-26T08:59:16.343110Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-11-26T08:59:16.342951Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-11-26T08:59:16.778213Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-11-26T08:59:16.777138Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1870x528 with 3 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    },
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "R² of batch on PC1/PC2 before: [np.float64(67.6), np.float64(69.8)]\n",
      "R² of batch on PC1/PC2 after: [np.float64(0.2), np.float64(2.2)]\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "def remove_batch_effect(Y, batch, design):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Y: stalen x eiwitten (geen NA). batch: categorisch. design: DataFrame met beschermde variabelen.\"\"\"\n",
    "    B = pd.get_dummies(batch, drop_first=True, dtype=float)\n",
    "    B = B - B.mean()                                       # gecentreerd: totaalgemiddelde blijft gelijk\n",
    "    D = pd.get_dummies(design, drop_first=True, dtype=float)\n",
    "    Xmat = np.column_stack([np.ones(len(Y)), D.values, B.values])\n",
    "    coef, *_ = np.linalg.lstsq(Xmat, Y.values, rcond=None)\n",
    "    batch_coef = coef[-B.shape[1]:, :]\n",
    "    return Y - B.values @ batch_coef\n",
    "\n",
    "beschermd = meta[[\"subject.ageGroup\", \"subject.biologicalSex\", \"cmv_status\"]]\n",
    "X_corr = remove_batch_effect(X, meta[\"olink_batch_id\"], beschermd)\n",
    "\n",
    "Xz_c = (X_corr - X_corr.mean()) / X_corr.std()\n",
    "pca_c = PCA(n_components=10).fit(Xz_c)\n",
    "scores_c = pd.DataFrame(pca_c.transform(Xz_c)[:, :2], index=X.index, columns=[\"PC1\", \"PC2\"]).join(meta)\n",
    "ve_c = pca_c.explained_variance_ratio_ * 100\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(17, 4.8))\n",
    "sns.scatterplot(data=pc, x=\"PC1\", y=\"PC2\", hue=\"olink_batch_id\", s=12, alpha=0.7, ax=axes[0])\n",
    "axes[0].set(title=\"Before correction - batch\", xlabel=f\"PC1 ({ve[0]:.1f}%)\", ylabel=f\"PC2 ({ve[1]:.1f}%)\")\n",
    "sns.scatterplot(data=scores_c, x=\"PC1\", y=\"PC2\", hue=\"olink_batch_id\", s=12, alpha=0.7, ax=axes[1])\n",
    "axes[1].set(title=\"After correction - batch\", xlabel=f\"PC1 ({ve_c[0]:.1f}%)\", ylabel=f\"PC2 ({ve_c[1]:.1f}%)\")\n",
    "sns.scatterplot(data=scores_c, x=\"PC1\", y=\"PC2\", hue=\"subject.ageGroup\", s=12, alpha=0.7, ax=axes[2])\n",
    "axes[2].set(title=\"After correction - age group\", xlabel=f\"PC1 ({ve_c[0]:.1f}%)\", ylabel=f\"PC2 ({ve_c[1]:.1f}%)\")\n",
    "for a in axes: a.legend(fontsize=7)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Hoeveel verklaart batch nog?\n",
    "for naam, s in [(\"before\", pc), (\"after\", scores_c)]:\n",
    "    print(f\"R² of batch on PC1/PC2 {naam}:\",\n",
    "          [round(smf.ols(f\"{p} ~ C(olink_batch_id)\", data=s).fit().rsquared * 100, 1) for p in [\"PC1\", \"PC2\"]])"
   ]
  },
